2-
3:Status: PLAN, 2026-11-24, written read-only against `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `4ae25a10` (snapshot extracted with `git archive`; nothing in the repo was edited). Unit rows: `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:83-85`; principle 4 ("Unattended means stricter", `:30`); gates G-3, G-4, G-6 (`:131-134`); decisions D15, D19, D21 (`:143,147,149`); phase C (`:118`). BG-3 is deferred to v1.4 by the plan and is not planned here. Verify every file:line by reading before you edit; line numbers drift.
4-
5-Acceptance (verbatim):
6-- **BG-1:** "kill the CLI, the run continues and resumes cleanly; the SI-7 kill test passes against the runner"
7-- **BG-2:** "a scheduled run on a seeded failing verifier ends BLOCKED and says so; an unattended run asking for approval is denied, not blocked forever; missed runs are reported, not silently skipped"
8-- **G-4:** "Unattended runs: tests show no allow-always, a fresh worktree, the unattended flag in receipts, and a kill-and-resume pass"
9-
10-Defaults taken (owner authorised autonomous decisions; recorded below): **D15** = documented `systemd --user` unit only, no self-daemonizing mode. **D19** = `read-only` by default, `worktree-write` per schedule (and per job) only with an explicit flag. **D21** = event triggers and SSH execution are v1.4; no work here. D21 does not defer time triggers: `cron`, `every` and `once` are BG-2's own scope.
11-
12-## 0. What exists (read, with citations)
13-
14-- **Durable operations are the unit a runner should own.** `nexus operation run|resume|decide|status|watch` (`cli/src/operation_cli.ts:299-581`). `run` validates the spec (`validateOperationSpec`, `:107`; unknown keys rejected, `SPEC_KEYS` `:80`), creates the record, optionally plans git isolation (`planOperationGit` + `ensureIntegrationWorktree`, `:333-345`), then calls the private `drive()` (`:257-282`): `driveOperation(op, {store, signal, entry, executor: new AgentWorkUnitExecutor({baseConfig: config})})`, SIGINT → abort, exit code 0 COMPLETE / 130 CANCELLED / 2 otherwise. Goals are operations too (`cli/src/goal.ts:1`, `GOAL_ID_PREFIX` `:10`).
15-- **Fresh worktrees exist.** `planOperationGit(workspace, operationId, baseRef)` (`cli/src/core/operation_git.ts:62-86`) puts every isolated operation under `<repo>/.nexus/worktrees/op-<key>/` with an integration branch `nexus/op-<key>/integration`. A new operation id therefore means fresh worktrees; the operator's checkout is never the unit workspace.
201-
202:Time triggers only (`cron`, `every`, `once`), evaluated by the runner. D21 keeps event triggers (file change, webhook) and SSH execution in v1.4, together with BG-3. Also out of v1.3.0: the optional deterministic wake `check` command (opencode `schedule/check.ts`; the acceptance does not need it, and it is another unattended code path), objective-ledger (goal) targets, time zones other than UTC, schedule spec files. A schedule fire creates a normal BG-1 job (`origin.kind = "schedule"`), so everything in §1 applies unchanged.
203-
204-### 3.2 Schedule record `nexus-schedule` v1 (`R/schedules/<id>.json`)
205-
206-```jsonc
207-{
208-  "format": "nexus-schedule", "schema_version": 1,
209-  "id": "nightly-lint",                    // [a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,39}, or sch-<8 hex>
210-  "createdAt": "…", "enabled": true,
211-  "workspace": "/real/repo",
212-  "trigger": { "kind": "cron", "expr": "0 3 * * 1-5" }   // 5 fields, UTC, numbers/*/ranges/steps/lists, no names
213-           | { "kind": "every", "seconds": 3600 }         // 300 ≤ seconds ≤ 30 days
214-           | { "kind": "once", "at": "2026-12-01T03:00:00Z" },
331-
332:BG-3 and D21 (file/webhook triggers, SSH/remote execution), wake `check` commands, time zones, schedule spec files, goal (objective-ledger) targets, live attach and multi-client streaming (PF-3), detaching `nexus run`/REPL sessions, Windows/macOS runners, auto-merge of job results, notifications (mail, webhooks), a system-wide (multi-user) runner.
333-
334-## Reference coding
335-
336-XERJ (local node, `systemctl --user is-active xerj` = active) has only the `opencode`, `awesome-ai-system-prompts` and `serverless-workflow-spec` corpora; goose, Cline and Codex are not indexed, so their parts come from `docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md:19-21` (read from source 2026-11-13/14/23). Queries: `xerj code opencode "schedule next_due_at remaining_runs last_outcome"` and `"schedule missed overdue catch up next_due_at advance"` (partial result lists: the node hit its deadline; the index is flagged "not verified complete"). **Took:** opencode's record fields (`nextDueAt`, `remainingRuns`, status, `packages/core/src/tool/plugin/schedule.ts` view) and its `every` rule "keep the phase: skip every missed slot rather than firing them in a burst" (`packages/core/src/schedule.ts` `following`, MIT, idea only). **Differs:** opencode skips missed slots silently; BG-2 counts and reports each one (acceptance). opencode stores a `tz`; v1.3.0 is UTC only. **Rejected:** goose's per-run `Auto` mode for scheduled runs (PLAN.md:21), opencode's in-process wake checks for now. No code copied.
337-
338-## Risks
339-
340-- **Approval semantics drift:** `UnattendedApprovalPolicy` is a second implementation of `requiresDecision`. Mitigation: it delegates the managed checks to the base class and its table is tested exhaustively; MT-2 or GV-1 changes to `ApprovalPolicy` must extend the table.
341-- **Useless-by-default jobs:** with exec denied, a `worktree-write` job can only run commands the operator allowed in `command_rules.json`; docs must show the pattern (allow `npm test`). Better to be blocked than to run unattended shell.
342-- **systemd cgroup kill** turns every runner crash into a worker crash; resume is the SI-7 path, so a crash mid-tool always needs a human. Accepted.
343-- **Upgrade friction:** the runner and workers hold shared client leases, so `nexus upgrade` waits; doctor and docs tell the operator to stop the runner.
